{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794559720590,"sessionID":"ses_e2be9abf0ffea6S3OJ4PZfZtpb","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4183a77001HDVQAFTst80M6c","sessionID":"ses_e2be9abf0ffea6S3OJ4PZfZtpb","messageID":"msg_1d4180b2d001cpM4vCHNWybECK","type":"tool","id":"call_4133c7395c6848ecbd544074","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"for f in foreign pure claude-only absent forked adopted stale; do echo \"--- $f\"; cat \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/fixtures/agents-md/$f/fixture.json\"; echo; done"},"output":"--- foreign\n{\n  \"name\": \"foreign\",\n  \"expect_state\": \"foreign\",\n  \"base\": \"own\",\n  \"own_document\": \"# Our own instructions\\n\\nThis repository predates the harness. Build with `make`, test with `make check`.\\n\\n## Local conventions\\n\\n- Keep every export beside its use.\\n- Never commit a generated file.\\n\",\n  \"files\": {},\n  \"notes\": \"A repository's own file. It carries no shipped section at all, so it is the repository's to keep and the template has to arrive around it.\"\n}\n\n--- pure\n{\n  \"name\": \"pure\",\n  \"expect_state\": \"pure\",\n  \"base\": \"template\",\n  \"block\": null,\n  \"files\": {},\n  \"notes\": \"Every shipped section current, no repository block. The document is rebuilt from the manifest's derived bodies, so it cannot describe a template the manifest does not ship.\"\n}\n\n--- claude-only\n{\n  \"name\": \"claude-only\",\n  \"expect_state\": \"claude-only\",\n  \"base\": \"none\",\n  \"files\": {\n    \"CLAUDE.md\": \"# Project notes\\n\\nRun `make check` before you open a pull request.\\n\"\n  },\n  \"notes\": \"No root document, one Claude-only file. The only instruction file this repository has is the one Claude reads second.\"\n}\n\n--- absent\n{\n  \"name\": \"absent\",\n  \"expect_state\": \"absent\",\n  \"base\": \"none\",\n  \"files\": {},\n  \"notes\": \"No instruction file of any kind, so nothing delivers the framework and nothing of the repository's own is at risk.\"\n}\n\n--- forked\n{\n  \"name\": \"forked\",\n  \"expect_state\": \"forked\",\n  \"base\": \"template\",\n  \"section_edits\": {\n    \"s6-spec-folder\": [\n      \"Local rule: name the packet in the first line of every pull request.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"insert_sections\": [\n    {\n      \"before\": \"s7-escalation\",\n      \"text\": \"## Local release checklist\\n\\nRun `make verify` and post the result in the release channel before tagging.\\n\\n\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"block\": null,\n  \"files\": {},\n  \"notes\": \"One local line inside a shipped section and one repository section between two shipped ones. Both sit past the delivery prefix so the fixture plants its two defects without also moving an anchor.\"\n}\n\n--- adopted\n{\n  \"name\": \"adopted\",\n  \"expect_state\": \"adopted\",\n  \"base\": \"template\",\n  \"block\": {\n    \"markers\": \"ordered\",\n    \"text\": \"\\nOur stack is Node 20 with no web framework.\\nBuild: `node --test scripts/`.\\nTest: `node --test scripts/` and `bash scripts/lint.sh`.\\n\"\n  },\n  \"files\": {\n    \"CLAUDE.md\": \"# Project notes\\n\\nRun `make check` before you open a pull request.\\nUpdate the changelog in the same commit as the code.\\n\"\n  },\n  \"notes\": \"Shipped sections current with a non-empty repository block, plus the hand-kept CLAUDE.md copy a repository that upgraded halfway keeps: two lines the root document does not carry.\"\n}\n\n--- stale\n{\n  \"name\": \"stale\",\n  \"expect_state\": \"stale\",\n  \"base\": \"template\",\n  \"replace_with_history\": [\"operational-mandates\"],\n  \"block\": null,\n  \"files\": {},\n  \"notes\": \"One shipped section still carries the body an earlier release shipped, so the repository is one release behind. The section is the document's last one, so replacing it moves no byte offset above it.\"\n}\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"--- foreign\n{\n  \"name\": \"foreign\",\n