ry section between two shipped ones. Both sit past the delivery prefix so the fixture plants its two defects without also moving an anchor.\"\n}\n\n--- adopted\n{\n  \"name\": \"adopted\",\n  \"expect_state\": \"adopted\",\n  \"base\": \"template\",\n  \"block\": {\n    \"markers\": \"ordered\",\n    \"text\": \"\\nOur stack is Node 20 with no web framework.\\nBuild: `node --test scripts/`.\\nTest: `node --test scripts/` and `bash scripts/lint.sh`.\\n\"\n  },\n  \"files\": {\n    \"CLAUDE.md\": \"# Project notes\\n\\nRun `make check` before you open a pull request.\\nUpdate the changelog in the same commit as the code.\\n\"\n  },\n  \"notes\": \"Shipped sections current with a non-empty repository block, plus the hand-kept CLAUDE.md copy a repository that upgraded halfway keeps: two lines the root document does not carry.\"\n}\n\n--- stale\n{\n  \"name\": \"stale\",\n  \"expect_state\": \"stale\",\n  \"base\": \"template\",\n  \"replace_with_history\": [\"operational-mandates\"],\n  \"block\": null,\n  \"files\": {},\n  \"notes\": \"One shipped section still carries the body an earlier release shipped, so the repository is one release behind. The section is the document's last one, so replacing it moves no byte offset above it.\"\n}\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"for f in foreign pure claude-only absent forked adopted stale; do echo \\\"--- $f\\\"; cat \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/fixtures/agents-md/$f/fixture.json\\\"; echo; done\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559720055,"end":1794559720590}}}}
